# @see ADR-167
id: TEST-034
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: Inconsistent test structure in same file
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .test.ts .test.js .spec.ts .spec.js .test.tsx .test.jsx
  exclude_paths: vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
  content_contains: describe
patterns:
  - regex: ^describe\(.*\n[\s\S]*\n\s*test\(
    message: "Mixed describe/it and standalone test() in same file — pick one pattern"
  - regex: \bit\(.*\n[\s\S]*\btest\(
    message: "File mixes it() and test() — use one consistently for readability"
fix: Choose one test structure per file. Use describe/it for BDD-style grouping, or standalone test() for flat structure. Mixing both makes the file harder to navigate and maintain. Configure your linter (eslint-plugin-jest consistent-test-it rule) to enforce one style.
